// Bun Snapshot v1, https://bun.sh/docs/test/snapshots

exports[`guided access step (T3) first run: Full Disk Access notice, Enter opens only its pane, then the Automation notice and the setup command 1`] = `
"
Step 1 of 2: Full Disk Access
🔐 Textbutler needs Full Disk Access to read your Messages.
   macOS doesn't ask for this. Turn on Textbutler in System Settings › Privacy & Security › Full Disk Access. Only the chats you pick are read.
   Press Enter to open Settings · s to skip
Turn on Textbutler in the list. If it isn't there, click +, press Command-Shift-G, enter ~/Applications/TextButler.app and choose Open.

Step 2 of 2: Automation
🔐 macOS will ask to let Textbutler control Messages.
   Textbutler only sends replies in chats you turn on. Change this any time in System Settings › Privacy & Security › Automation.
   App setup shows this notice again before macOS asks.
Stop the background service, then run app setup from your Textbutler source folder:
  bun run textbutler:app imessage-setup --data-dir '/Volumes/Data/Application Support/Textbutler'
→ Then choose Setup & readiness (1) to check the result.
"
`;

exports[`guided access step (T3) an Automation denial shows the recovery, and o opens only the Automation pane 1`] = `
"
Step 2 of 2: Automation
✗ Textbutler can't control Messages: macOS access is off for Textbutler.
  Turn on Textbutler in System Settings › Privacy & Security › Automation.
→ press o to open Settings, then run app setup again
Stop the background service, then run app setup from your Textbutler source folder:
  bun run textbutler:app imessage-setup --data-dir '/Volumes/Data/Application Support/Textbutler'
→ Then choose Setup & readiness (1) to check the result.
"
`;
